# The first rule that matches a path wins, so every exact rule sits above the wildcards (Cloudflare asks for that
# order too), and every old URL reaches its page in one hop.

# The tea room is being rebuilt. Until the new page is finished, /tea/ leads to its working copy, at the owner's
# word (2026-11-13). 302, not 301: /tea/ will be the new page's own address again, so no browser may keep this.
# The old page still builds at /tea/ (its tests still hold it) and is no longer reached on the live site, where a
# redirect is followed before a file is looked for; it is kept whole at /labs/tea-room/v1/.
/tea /labs/tea-room/working/ 302
/tea/ /labs/tea-room/working/ 302

